# Screen composition

Screen files stay thin. Do not grow multi-screen barrels or 400+ line screen modules.

## Layout

```
src/features/<feature>/
  screens/<Name>Screen.tsx
  components/<Name>.tsx
  hooks/use<Name>.ts
  index.ts
```

## Rules

- One exported screen per `screens/*Screen.tsx` file.
- Move JSX sections into `components/`.
- Move fetching, selectors, derived values, and handlers into `hooks/`.
- Keep styles colocated with the owning file.
- Navigators import from feature barrels or `screens/` — not mega `*Screens.tsx`.
- Do not reach into another feature's private internals; use that feature's public export.

## Target size

- Prefer screens under ~200 lines.
- Prefer components under ~150 lines.
- Prefer hooks under ~120 lines.

## Loading

- Use design `Skeleton` / `EmptyState` / `ErrorState` for fetch loading / empty / retry.
- Use `Button` disabled + label for submits and mutations.
- Do not show “empty” or “unavailable” while the first load is still in flight.
